# L §6.1: "A member's asks are asked inside the joint model as a.q; since imports are pinned and never changed, joining
# changes no member's answer"; E §3.1 step 1: a member is all its files, its scenario files included ("A reality's hash
# covers every file", L §6.1). The member a of L6_1_member_directory (doubled stating `at reader`, since in s the rate
# changes with the law date, L §6.4) with asks in its scenario file: a.sq and a.sb are asked by the member alone in its
# world s (L §6.4 Asking: "An ask names its world"), where s_rate replaces the rate with 0.5 from 2026-06-01: doubled =
# 0.5 + 0.5 = 1 at law date 2026-12-31 (a.sq), and the base's 0.12 + 0.12 = 0.24 at a law date before the divergence day
# (a.sb, L §6.4 "nothing before it changes"). (Was REFCORE-NOT-YET: a member's ask in one of its scenario files.)
=== J/joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "../A" sha256 "a3dfeb5088ae8be31aff6ae9e0642855cedf5227e6cb47ac6adad292eab71a1c"

ask r: a.rate
=== A/reality.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

def doubled: num = rate + rate at reader
=== A/law/pit.tally
part pit
  tally 2
  law

source act "ustawa"

input rate: num

version pit_2026
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.12 "art. 1"
=== A/asks/q.tally
part asks
  tally 2

ask q: doubled law 2026-03-31
=== A/scenarios/s.tally
scenario s over ana
  tally 2
  from 2026-06-01

version s_rate
  cite act
  governs 2026-06-01..
  known 2025-01-01
  replace rate = 0.5 "scenariusz"

ask sq: doubled in s law 2026-12-31
ask sb: doubled in s law 2026-03-31
=== expect r a.q a.sq a.sb
r: 0.12
  cut 2026-10-20
a.q: 0.24
  law date 2026-03-31, cut 2026-10-20
a.sq: 1
  world: s
  held: rate = 0.5 (s_rate), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
a.sb: 0.24
  world: s
  law date 2026-03-31, cut 2026-10-20
